Z||000000||scrubbs||04-25-2000||12:08 AM||||im in grade 12 and looking fo a car that will get me to university and that i can have a little bit of fun with.  Can i have some general info and specs on the earlier fieros, i dont have that much to spend so nothin too extreme. Any recomendations? Anything i should stay away from?  Ive seen some cheap ones for sale, like $1500 canadian, about $1000US. how are they on gas, i got to go a long way, so ones that have better gas mileage, would be better, and any help would be appreciated||||reg||5
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||04-25-2000||10:19 AM||||My best recomendation, Scrubbs, would be an 87 or 88 4 clyinder 5 speed coupe. My 87 coupe gets about 32 mpg. One thing to watch, however, is the clutch. Try to look for one one that has recently been redone. The clutch job is rather involved and can be expensive. The other thing about the 87-88 model 4 clyinder models is the crankfire ignition system which I feel is much more reliable than the older distributor models. GOOD LUCK !!! I love my little car and you will too if you find the right one.<p>[This message has been edited by 2M4 Dale (edited 04-25-2000).]||||reg||14
